      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "All essential Theorem1.9 support was read: indeterminacy1.7(i), coefficient/matrix setup and Fubini inversion Lemma2.1, moment-coefficient recurrences3.3-3.6 with the eventually q-increasing comparison3.7, inverse coefficient recurrence/shift estimates4.1-4.5, Corollary4.6 and the complete superexponential summability proof5.1. The author separately controls normalized moments U_n and reproducing-kernel diagonal coefficients V_n via two q-Pochhammer induction bounds, handles finite initial perturbations, and obtains c_(2n-j)*s_(2n) decay. This proves the strong cs-star summability condition, which the supplied absolute-double-sum argument turns into the reproducing-kernel inverse identity. All other log-concave thresholds, birth-death counterexample and explicit classical-family variants are uncounted."
      },
      "extra_source_paths": [
        "raw/sigma-2018-109-137/paper-109-source/sigma18-109.tex",
        "raw/sigma-2018-109-137/paper-109-source.zip"
      ],
      "statement_scope": "Full Theorem1.9 for a symmetric Hamburger probability-moment problem with infinite support and all moments, Jacobi diagonal a_n=0, positive recurrence b_n, and b_(n-1)/b_n<=q for some0<q<1 and all sufficiently large n. Retain definitions U_n=s_(2n)/(b_0^2...b_(n-1)^2), V_n=b_0...b_(n-1)*c_n and c_n=sqrt(A_(n,n)), where A is the reproducing-kernel coefficient matrix. U_n,V_n,c_n*sqrt(s_(2n)) are bounded and sum_l c_l*abs(s_(l+m)) is finite for every m>=0. The supplied Lemma2.1 yields AH=HA=I with entrywise absolute convergence. No bounded-operator inverse interpretation on l2, uniqueness among all infinite inverses or polynomial-growth relaxation is added.",
      "admission_hold": false,
      "proof_complete": true,
      "contexts": [],
      "id": "1817",
      "doi": "10.3842/SIGMA.2018.109",
      "status": "native_tex_ready",
